00:10:26,666 --> 00:10:32,666
The Boy in the Striped Pyjamas is a drama, war,
history film directed by Mark Herman.

3
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:46,000
When his family moves from their home in Berlin to a strange new house in Poland, young Bruno befriends Shmuel, a
boy who lives on the other side of the fence where everyone seems to be wearing striped pajamas.

4
00:20:53,333 --> 00:20:59,333
Unaware of Shmuel's fate as a Jewish prisoner or the role his own Nazi father plays in his
imprisonment, Bruno embarks on a dangerous journey inside the camp's walls.

5
00:26:06,666 --> 00:26:12,666
Bruno, played by Asa Butterfield.

6
00:31:20,000 --> 00:31:26,000
Mother, played by Vera Farmiga.

7
00:36:33,333 --> 00:36:39,333
Father, played by David Thewlis.

8
00:41:46,666 --> 00:41:52,666
Shmuel, played by Jack Scanlon.

9
00:47:00,000 --> 00:47:06,000
Gretel, played by Amber Beattie.

10
00:52:13,333 --> 00:52:19,333
Lieutenant Kotler, played by Rupert Friend.

11
00:57:26,666 --> 00:57:32,666
The Boy in the Striped Pyjamas (released as The Boy in the Striped Pajamas in North America)
is a 2008 Holocaust historical drama film written and directed by Mark Herman.

12
01:02:40,000 --> 01:02:46,000
It is based on the 2006 novel of the same name by John Boyne.

13
01:07:53,333 --> 01:07:59,333
Set in Nazi-occupied Poland, the film follows the son of a Schutzstaffel
(SS) officer who befriends a Jewish prisoner of his age.

14
01:13:06,666 --> 01:13:12,666
It was released in the United Kingdom on 12 September 2008.

15
01:18:20,000 --> 01:18:26,000
It received generally positive reviews from critics for its emotional weight, mature themes and
acting but was panned by scholars for misrepresenting elements of the Holocaust.

16
01:23:33,333 --> 01:23:39,333
The film explores themes of based on novel or book, nazi,
nationalism, concentration camp, world war ii.

17
01:28:46,666 --> 01:28:52,666
The tone is emotional.
